Rule Name: Task
Description: 
Software Engineer Assignment
This assignment is designed to assess your full-stack development skills by leveraging a Weather API to
build a meteorological research tool for plant care. The objective is to build a user-friendly application that
manages end-to-end plant care for a given-user using React and Typescript.
Requirements
1. Basic Backend
1. Write a basic backend that can store plant information
2. Display all brands for the user on the front end
3. This application should support world-wide plant-care
2. Add/Edit Brands
1. Users should be able to add new plants
2. Users can delete or edit existing plants.
3. Plants have the following metadata: Type of Plant, Weekly Water Need, Expected
Relative Humidity (%)
3. Front end Display Functionality
1. Users must be able to see an automatic evaluation of their plants health – based on the
expected water amount/humidity vs. the real rain amount/humidity
1. You can use any method for this, but here is a free-API: https://open-meteo.com/
en/docs/historical-forecast-api
2. Users must be able to see a historical chart of the health of their plants
3. If the user edits the plants metadata the historical chart must display a change in
“expected” water or humidity
4. Allow users to see how well their plant has done at specific periods of times with an
ability to select unique date ranges
Bonus Features
1. Produce support for multiple house-holds (meaning user can have plants in a variety of locations)
2. Add searching and filtering based on metadata and name
3. Provide pagination for customer with over 15 plants
Expectations
Completing every requirement of the assignment is not mandatory. The key objective is to showcase your
ability to deliver innovative and value-added solutions. The focus should not be limited to merely fulfilling
the listed requirements but rather on demonstrating creativity and developing exceptional solutions.
Key Guidelines:
1. Technology Flexibility: You may use any technology of your choice to complete the assignment,
allowing you to leverage your strengths and preferred tools.
2. Docker Usage: Using Docker is highly recommended to ensure consistency, ease of
deployment, and scalability.
3. Documentation: Provide a clear and concise README document that explains:
◦ How the code works.
◦ Instructions for setting up and running the project.
◦ Any design decisions or key considerations in your implementation.
1. Commit Quality: Ensure that commits and commit messages are neat, descriptive,
and reflect the progress and rationale behind your work.
Key Criteria for Evaluation:
1. Innovation: Prioritize unique and impactful approaches over simply meeting all technical
requirements.
2. Scalability: Solutions that are scalable and designed to handle growth will be highly regarded.
3. Efficiency: Deliver performant and optimized implementations for both the back end and front
end.
4. Value Addition: Enhance the assignment with features or improvements that go beyond the
original scope, adding tangible value.
